From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:39:37 +0900
Subject: GPU plugin: Qualcomm Adreno through the KGSL driver

Android kernels drive the Adreno GPU with the downstream KGSL driver: there is /dev/kgsl-3d0 and
/sys/class/kgsl/kgsl-3d0, but no DRM device, so the Linux backend found no GPU, gpu/all/usage did
not exist and System Monitor's Overview and History pages said "This page is missing some
sensors" (docs/104).
LinuxBackend now adds a LinuxKgslGpu when /sys/class/kgsl/kgsl-3d0/gpu_model is readable:
name from gpu_model ("Adreno710v1" -> "Adreno 710"); usage from the growth of the cumulative busy
microseconds of gpu_clock_stats over the elapsed time (gpubusy, the busy share of the last powered
second, when that is unreadable; never devfreq/gpu_load, which resets the governor's statistics on
read); frequency from devfreq/cur_freq within available_frequencies; temperature from temp
(millidegrees). The memory is unified, so no video memory figures; no power. Files are read only
for subscribed sensors. Parsing in KgslStats with tests (kgsltest, values from an Adreno 710).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic for KGSL kernels; upstream MR !149 covers msm DRM only]
X-Rungic-Tests: L1:kgsltest
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/104
